<header class="post-header">
<p class="help-kicker"><a href="/blog/category/on-page-seo/">On-page SEO</a><span class="help-step">Step 1 of 2</span></p>
<h1>Why internal links matter</h1>
<p class="dek">Internal links help readers and search engines find the rest of your site. Here is how to add them without overthinking it.</p>
<div class="post-meta">
<p class="post-date">Updated <time datetime="2026-10-20">20 October 2026</time></p>
<p class="reading-time"><time datetime="PT1M">1 min read</time></p>
<address>By <a rel="author" href="/blog/authors/asif/">Asif</a></address>
</div>
<div class="help-before">
<p class="help-before-title">Before you start</p>
<dl>
<div>
<dt>Time</dt>
<dd>12 minutes</dd>
</div>
<div>
<dt>Level</dt>
<dd>Easy</dd>
</div>
</dl>
</div>
</header>
<details class="toc-inline">
<summary>On this page</summary>
<nav aria-label="On this page">
<ol class="toc-nested">
<li><a href="#readers-use-them-to-keep-going">Readers use them to keep going</a></li>
<li><a href="#search-engines-use-them-to-find-and-rank-pages">Search engines use them to find and rank pages</a></li>
